-- The 54 ICD "LLU" zones — a distinct internal numbering ICD uses for point-radius
-- prohibited-flight zones specifically closing the loophole that would otherwise let
-- micro/mini drones (≤250g) fly near these sites under the general exemptions for that
-- weight class. Every single one states "אסור לטיסה ברדיוס X מטר" (flight prohibited
-- within a stated radius) — legally the same PROHIBITED category as LLP, just under
-- ICD's own catalog rather than a PMAT LL-code. No ceiling is stated beyond the shared
-- category note (500m/1,000ft as a default), so — as agreed — these import as
-- ground-blocked (no known ceiling) rather than guessing a number.

